# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-11, pick P26). A line fanned over axis combinations that give one result prints it once,
# under [pick = *] (L §5.5), and its register names the union of the unknown days of every combination it stands for,
# by rule (L §8.2): wd[a] under a, wd[b] under b, one equal hole.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
=== m.tally
model fan
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
axis pick
  a "first"
  b "second"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pay: money PLN
input wd[p in pick]: date

def dday: date = wd[pick]

move pay_p: transfers
  on dday
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd[a] = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  wd[b] = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask f1: bal(konto, 2026-03-06)
=== expect
f1 [pick = a]: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_p" (wd[a])
  unknown day: wd[a]
  reading: pick = a
  cut 2026-01-10
f1 [pick = b]: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_p" (wd[b])
  unknown day: wd[b]
  reading: pick = b
  cut 2026-01-10
